# two literals of texts, each stored one more name behind its allocation. Where boxed slots leave a word of the cell, the first late name of the layout lies there, and no field that lies in the cell with boxed slots leaves it because forms get narrower:
# it counts like any slot where the chooser asks whether the cell gets smaller.
# the pair: two boxed texts and the late name fill a cell of 48. Narrow, the three end at 32 behind the header and the hidden word, the first of them beside that word: a cell of 32, and the late name is in it.
# the four: four boxed texts and the late name fill a cell of 64, with narrow texts one of 48: one text lies beside the hidden word, two lie narrow behind the one that may stay boxed, and the late name follows at the next multiple of eight in the form of its own.
# -- source: late-name-in-the-word-that-boxed-slots-leave-stays-in-the-cell.js
